## Scope Contract 1: Root Products Page Fix

**Goal:** Fix the "/products" root page to correctly display all products

### Current State
```typescript
// app/(store)/products/page.tsx:39
const path = ["products"]; // ❌ Invalid VFS keys
const [productsResult] = await Promise.all([
  getSelectedProducts(path, ...) // Returns zero products
]);
```

### Target State
```typescript
// Option A: Empty array triggers "all products" query
const catalogueKeys: string[] = []; // ✅ Empty = all products
const [productsResult] = await Promise.all([
  getSelectedProducts(catalogueKeys, ...) // Returns all products
]);
```

### Implementation
1. **Update `getSelectedProducts.ts`**:
   - Handle empty `catalogueKeys` array as "all products" query
   - Remove `categoryPath` constraint when keys are empty
   - Maintain existing filter/sort/pagination logic

2. **Update `app/(store)/products/page.tsx`**:
   - Pass empty array instead of `["products"]`
   - Update page title to "All Products"
   - Verify filter/sortables still function

### DoD - Verification Checklist
- [ ] `/products` page displays all products from Sanity
- [ ] Empty `catalogueKeys` array returns complete product catalog
- [ ] Filters and sortables function on root products page
- [ ] Pagination works correctly
- [ ] No regression on category-specific pages

### Testing
```bash
# Verify all products returned
# 1. Start dev server: npm run dev
# 2. Navigate to /products
# 3. Verify product count matches Sanity total
# 4. Apply filters, verify subset returned
# 5. Navigate to /products/headphones/open-back
# 6. Verify only open-back products shown (no regression)
```

